<title>USA: UAW to vote on tentative pact at Alcoa.</title>
<headline>UAW to vote on tentative pact at Alcoa.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Members of United Autoworkers union will vote Friday on a tentative five-year labor pact reached with Aluminum Co of America that will end a 22-day strike if approved, an Alcoa spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed. The tentative agreement was reached after an extended bargaining session led by a federal mediator.</p>
<p>The strike has been ongoing by 1,100 members of UAW Local 1050 at Alcoa's forging plant in Cleveland. The plant makes forged aluminum parts for industries including aerospace and automotive.</p>
<p>--Pittsburgh newsroom 412-471-7088</p>
